  "ui.turretdefense.help_title": "Turret Guide",
  "ui.turretdefense.back_machine": "Back to Machine",
  "ui.turretdefense.details_title": "Turret Head Details",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_intro": "Install a core and base, then mount a head. This guide explains operation; current values depend on the machine and server configuration.",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_install_title": "1. Installation and Binding",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_install_body": "Place a Base Core, then a Turret Base within its management range. Close the screen and right-click a free base face while holding a turret head. The adjacent block must be empty. Heads mount on bases.\nT1/T2/T3/T4/T5 bases support 1/2/3/4/6 heads. Bind the base to a core with the same owner to receive supplies.",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_power_title": "2. Energy and Shutdown",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_power_body": "Put valid fuel such as coal in the core fuel slot, or input FE. The core supplies bound bases. Idle operation, attacks, repair and shields consume energy. A mounted head still requires sufficient ongoing power.\nLow energy can trigger power saving or shutdown. Check core energy, base energy, binding and the external power supply. Low energy and missing ammunition are separate conditions.",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_ammo_title": "3. Ammunition Storage and Type",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_ammo_body": "Store ammunition in the core's 18-slot ammunition inventory. Bases have no ammunition slots. T1–T3 heads use no ammunition. Check Required Ammunition in head details for higher tiers. Laser heads require no ammunition.\nHeads requiring ammunition also consume FE. Other ammunition types cannot substitute for the requested type. Check type, quantity and binding when a head reports missing ammunition.",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_upgrade_title": "4. Tier Upgrades",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_upgrade_body": "Craft T1 machines at a crafting table. Upgrade higher tiers through the corresponding machine screen. Prepare all listed materials and energy; materials are reserved from the operator's inventory and FE can be paid over time.\nReserved materials leave the player's inventory. Cancellation returns the materials but does not refund paid FE. Base tier determines head capacity; upgrading a head does not add base capacity. JEI lists upgrade materials.",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_modules_title": "5. Base Plugins and Core Modules",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_modules_body": "Base modules are shared by all attached heads. T1–T5 unlock 1–5 slots with at most one special module. There are 37 effects and 63 graded items. Ordinary head destruction retains modules; core detonation settles drops. Core upgrades use 5 separate slots unlocked by core tier, with duplicate categories disabled by default.",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_defense_title": "6. Core Defense and Shields",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_defense_body": "With sufficient energy the core provides shields, projection and area deflection. Incoming projectiles are reflected without recreation; allied shots are protected and efficiency drops at low power. Phase turrets and camouflage modules can hide heads. Arbiters have two modes; other heads require a mode module and switch from the details page.",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_automation_title": "7. Loot and Automation",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_automation_body": "Every 5 seconds the core checks loaded blocks in a 5×5×5 region and outputs loot, bottles first. With AE2 it prioritizes active grids owned by the owner or trusted players, refills required advanced ammunition and converts a configured fraction of AE to FE. It does not force-load chunks or export fuel and core modules.",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_troubleshooting_title": "8. Installation and Firing Problems",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_troubleshooting_body": "Cannot install: check that you are clicking a base, holding a head, using a free face with empty adjacent space, below base capacity, and authorized to operate it.\nUnbound: check mounting, core range and owner.\nNo target: check for eligible enemies within effective range.\nBlocked: clear the muzzle path or check that turret type's trajectory rules.\nOverheated / waiting for firing budget: wait for recovery. Clicking repeatedly does not force firing.\nUpgrade failed: check materials, maximum tier, any ongoing upgrade and permission. If text is crowded, adjust GUI scale and scroll inside the panel.",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_details_title": "9. Head Details",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_details_body": "Open an installed head's details from the base screen to inspect tier, health, shields, status, target priority, attack parameters, ammunition, mode, shared plugins, kills and upgrade materials.\nUse the six face buttons to inspect other faces. Empty faces show no installed head. Back restores the machine screen. The guide itself consumes no items or energy.",
  "ui.turretdefense.help_connection_hint": "Machines continue running while this guide is open. Return to the machine screen to use inventory or upgrade controls.",
  "ui.turretdefense.details_waiting": "Waiting for machine state. If the machine was removed or is too far away, reopen its screen.",
  "ui.turretdefense.details_empty": "No turret head is installed on this face, or it was removed.",
